Description: Return seeded contacts from a private Kad mesh KADEMLIA2_RES.
 CRoutingBin::GetClosestTo() filters returned contacts by
 GetType() <= maxType && IsIPVerified(). In a small air-gapped interop mesh the
 seeded contacts never age to a good type nor complete IP verification, so aMule
 withholds every one and answers each KADEMLIA2_REQ with an empty (count=0)
 KADEMLIA2_RES, making distance-ordering evidence uncapturable.
 .
 This relaxes only that return-filter. The ordering is computed separately and is
 NOT touched: each returned contact map key is targetDistance = ClientID ^ target,
 sorted by CUInt128 comparison -- genuine aMule XOR distance. The set of returned
 contacts grows to include the seeded ones; their order stays real aMule output
 (ADR-0043). maxType stays referenced (short-circuit)
 to avoid an unused-parameter warning. Private interop evidence capture only.
Author: rmule interop harness
Forwarded: not-needed
